Z||000016||artherd||09-07-2001||06:14 PM||||Hey Formula, so far so good with those two major hurdles (biggest is the ECU.)<P>Don't worry, the world will know all about it once she's done, I'm making a webiste on the process.  <P>Yeah, a sports car withought a 5-speed (stick) just dosen't do it for me, and I love big 4-cam engines, and the Northstar will bolt right up withought any adapter plates and only very slight mods.   mmmm...<P>It's like this engine was made for this car, its going easier so far than putting a v6 back in, lol!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>The two reasons I always say I won't do a N* over a SBC is because of getting the electronics ironed out and no 5 speed.  Hmm, seems you've covered both of those concerns.  I'm VERY interested to see how this turns out.<P>I would love to get an itemized shopping list and prices when you're done.  Any help you pioneers can give the rest of us when we venture forth is greatly appreciated!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
